.SH "Enumeration Type Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "enum \fBaction_flags\fP"
.PP
context for an action selected from the context-menu. 
.PP
this is interesting mostly when the action is to be applied to a seletion of several objects. 
.PP
\fBEnumerator: \fP
.in +1c
.TP
\fB\fIAF_NONE \fP\fP
no flags 
.TP
\fB\fIAF_YES_TO_ALL \fP\fP
'yes to all', stop asking 
.TP
\fB\fIAF_CANCEL_ALL \fP\fP
'no to all', stop asking 
.TP
\fB\fIAF_SELECTION \fP\fP
selection set on action-context (multiple files) 
.TP
\fB\fIAF_MENUDONE \fP\fP
terminate menu-loop 
.TP
\fB\fIAF_LAST \fP\fP
last item to process, free any resources. 
.PP
plugins using this should check this last thing before returning (specifically, after any calls to \fBform_yes_no_all()\fP) 
